# What `COPY . .` must never pick up.
#
# Two reasons, in order: secrets, then size. Without this file the build
# context carried `.env` (every secret this app has), the uploaded media, the
# local node_modules and .next, and the whole git history — and the build stage
# baked all of it into an image layer, where `docker history` and anyone who
# pulls the image can read it.
#
# The build needs package*.json, prisma/, src/, messages/, scripts/, public/
# and the root config files. Everything below is something it does not.

# Secrets. The example is harmless, but nothing in the image reads it either.
.env
.env.*

# Rebuilt inside the image, for the image's platform.
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Runtime data: lives in a volume, never in the image.
media
public/uploads

# Tests, test output and saved end-to-end sessions (which hold a signed-in
# cookie).
tests
e2e
test-results
playwright-report
coverage
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.ts

# Repository and tooling state. `.claude` holds agent worktrees: whole copies
# of the repository, secrets and node_modules included.
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*

# Documentation and the files that describe the image rather than go in it.
docs
*.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
